# Cursor Rules for Fisher

Before planning or making any changes:
1. Read `AGENTS.md` - this is the universal operating directive for all AI agents.
2. Read `log.md` - review the execution history, recent code modifications, test runs, and handoff notes from previous agents.
3. Read `plan.md` - understand the architectural design and phase exit gates.
4. Run `pytest -v` to confirm baseline test suite passes.
5. After finishing work, always append a structured session entry to `log.md` under "Agent Execution History & Handoff Log".
